    "created_at": "2026-06-02T23:14:55Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-06-02T23:14:55Z",
    "body": "Some things:\n- Is a placeholder option for size=1 web compatible?\n- for single-select the placeholder option or any other option is deselected when selecting a new option, this logic I think is not present for select-multiple, so currently the placeholder options would remain selected when selecting other options.\nMaybe additional logic can be added to deselect the placeholder when selecting options and reselect the placeholder when none are selected.\n- with the hypothetical logic above, clicking the placeholder would deselect all the options?\n- UAs that render a listbox for size=1,  is another thing to consider.\n\n@mtrootyy do you have any particular expectation or usecase?\nNote that using css with `<button>` and `<selectedcontent>` is it possible to display what you want when no options are selected using `:empty` class and sibling selectors(`~` `+`) or `:has()`.\n\n@josepharhar I think for now is better to revert the removal of \"does not have a multiple attribute specified\", maybe in https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12069 ?",
