    "created_at": "2026-06-08T23:24:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-06-08T23:24:12Z",
    "body": "Having a placeholder option is useful because of these reasons/behaviors for single-select elements, right?\n- It is selected by default whether it has the selected attribute or not because it comes first\n- It can contain text guiding the user to choose another one of the options\n- It can have the hidden attribute to prevent the user from selecting the placeholder again\n- When choosing another option, the placeholder becomes deselected\n\nI think that supporting placeholder options for `<select multiple size=1>` would be cool, especially to make the selectedcontent element work better, but I'm not sure that it would be great if you can simultaneously select the placeholder option and other options. Do others agree? It would take some work to make that happen, but its probably doable. Should the placeholder option also automatically become re-selected when all other options are deselected?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
