    "updated_at": "2026-06-09T12:39:57Z",
    "body": "I think that if we define the **placeholder ~~label~~ option** as:\n\n*A placeholder option is an option intended to represent the absence of a user choice.*\n\nthen much of the behavior follows naturally from that definition.\n\n> Should the placeholder option also automatically become re-selected when all other options are deselected?\n\nI think it should.\nAlso, selecting the placeholder should deselect all other options.\n\n---\n\nRegarding the title of this issue, I fail to understand why a placeholder option is required for single-select. ~~Even several examples in the spec do not have one...~~\n\n---\n\nAnother thing that would be nice is support for a placeholder option in select listboxes (size>1). I think that would likely require additional syntax for web compatibility reasons, something like:\n\n```html\n<select multiple size=4>\n  <option value=\"\" placeholder>something</option>\n  ...\n</select>\n```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
