    "body": "I have divagated a bit from the OP, sorry.\nOP is saying `<select multiple size=1 required>` must have a placeholder option.\nI dont see any reason to why, UAs seem to already handle the `select fallback button text` well, and even without a placeholder option the validity aspect works well.\n\n---\n\n> Is there a good example of a listbox with a placeholder option out there on the web? As in something that doesn't actually use the select element. I can't think of a good use case for this.\n\nI'm not sure. My thought was that if a listbox was being used as a primitive to build a custom dropdown/select component, a placeholder option could be useful for replicating the behavior of a native select element,\nbut it doesn't seem necessary, because listbox can have no options selected.\n\nAnother possibility is a multi-select listbox where one option effectively means \"clear all selections.\" I've seen similar patterns in the wild, though not usually implemented as an actual option within the listbox.\nThough I'm not sure whether an option is the best pattern for that, a button might make more sense.\n\n---\n\nFor now, I would suggest figuring out placeholder options for `<select size=1 multiple>` in a new issue.\n\nAnother thing I thought of was to maybe decouple the placeholder definition from `required`...\nAlso now the spec is in a funky state, we need to fix that at some point.\n",
